  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Dr.D is now fond of matrices. He is particularly interested in Doofish Matrices. A Doofish Matrix of order NNN is a matrix with NNN rows (numbered 111 through NNN) and NNN columns (numbered 111 through NNN) such that:\n\n\nEach element of this matrix is an integer between 111 and 2N−12N-12N−1 inclusive.\nFor each iii and jjj (1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N, 1≤j≤2N−11 \\le j \\le 2N-11≤j≤2N−1), the integer jjj appears in the iii-th row and/or in the iii-th column.\nNow, for a given NNN, Dr.D is wondering if there is a Doofish Matrix of order NNN. Find such a matrix or determine that it does not exist. If there are multiple solutions, you may find any one.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤2,0001 \\le T \\le 2,0001≤T≤2,000",
      "1≤N≤2,0001 \\le N \\le 2,0001≤N≤2,000",
      "the sum of N2N^2N2 over all test cases does not exceed 4⋅1064 \\cdot 10^64⋅106",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (29 points):** NNN is a power of 222"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case:\n\n\nFirst, print a line containing the string `\"Hooray\"` if a Doofish Matrix of order NNN exists or `\"Boo\"` if it does not.\nIf it exists, print NNN more lines describing one such matrix. For each valid iii, the iii-th of these lines should contain NNN space-separated integers ― the elements in the iii-th row.",
    "notes": [],
